<BaseLayout title="About the project">
  <div class="wrap static-page"><span class="eyebrow">Our story</span><h1>A window into a living culture.</h1><div class="prose">
  <p>Chinese Culture Atlas is an independent learning project for curious people around the world. We make thoughtful introductions to festivals, arts, language, literature and everyday practices.</p>
  <h2>What we believe</h2><p>Culture is not one fixed narrative. Practices vary across regions, communities, families and generations. A good introduction should help readers see that variety rather than reduce it to stereotypes.</p>
  <p>We distinguish between historical evidence, traditional stories and modern customs; we include reading links to help you go deeper. This website is educational, not an official cultural institution.</p>
  <h2>How to begin</h2><p>Try our <a href="/learn/">beginner lessons</a>, browse the <a href="/culture/">culture library</a>, or read about a <a href="/festivals/">festival</a>.</p>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Editorial note.</strong> The site is in its first development phase. Further independent subject review and a public feedback contact channel are planned before full launch.</div>
  </div></div>
</BaseLayout>
